/**
\fn Serializer Serializer::setResourceMode(int mode)
\brief Choose embedded image resources or permit external resource references.
\param mode `pdg.serialization_Complete` (the default) embeds pixels;
`pdg.serialization_ExternalReferences` permits named file/resource references.
\return This Serializer for chaining.

The policy belongs to this writer. Set it before writing data; changing the policy
after writing begins throws. Unknown constants, fractional values and non-numbers
throw without changing the policy. Image records identify their representation,
so readers need no matching option.

Complete records load without their original files or resource cache. Reference
records resolve the original file path or ResourceManager resource name on load.
Missing resources and changed dimensions throw with the resource identifier.
Anonymous runtime images and images whose pixels have been modified are embedded
in either mode. Frame layout, opacity, edge clamping and subsection/frame selection
are preserved. Initial Sprite frame records use the same policy for artwork and collision masks.
Resource policy does not change the flags selecting object state.

\note Runtime-created and modified images retain their pixels. Named images can
reload their pixels during a complete save; call Image::retainData() before drawing
if the source will become unavailable before saving. Missing pixels produce an
explicit save error; complete mode never silently falls back to a reference.
Discard the writer after a failed serialization operation.

\code{.js}
// image is an existing pdg.Image or pdg.ImageStrip.
const writer = new pdg.Serializer();
writer.setResourceMode(pdg.serialization_Complete);
image.serialize(writer);
const saved = writer.getDataPtr();
// Select pdg.serialization_ExternalReferences on a new writer to permit
// smaller records that reload their named resources.
\endcode
\sa Serializer::getResourceMode(), Image::serialize()
*/

/**
\fn int Serializer::getResourceMode()
\brief Return the resource policy selected for this writer.
\return `pdg.serialization_Complete` or `pdg.serialization_ExternalReferences`.
*/

/**
\fn uint Image::getSerializedSize(Serializer serializer)
\brief Measure an image record using this writer's resource policy.
\param serializer Destination writer used for sizing.
\return Image record size in bytes, excluding the stream header and enclosing object tag/length.
Sizing validates availability of embedded pixels and may reload a named image.
Embedded records support RGB/RGBA pixels, dimensions up to 32768 on each axis,
and at most 512 MiB of pixel data.
\sa Image::serialize(), Serializer::setResourceMode()
*/

/**
\fn undefined Image::serialize(Serializer serializer)
\brief Save this image with pixels or a resolvable resource reference.
\param serializer Destination writer; its resource mode selects the representation.
Frame layout, opacity, edge clamping and subsection selection are included.
Anonymous runtime images and modified pixels embed in either mode. This writes a
raw record; restore it by calling Image::deserialize() on an existing image.
\sa Serializer::setResourceMode(), Image::getSerializedSize()
*/

/**
\fn undefined Image::deserialize(Deserializer deserializer)
\brief Replace this image from a saved image record.
\param deserializer Reader positioned at a raw image record written by Image::serialize().
The saved record determines whether pixels are embedded or resources must be
resolved. Missing resources, changed resource dimensions and malformed data throw.
The old image content remains unchanged on validation failure. Decoded pixels and
shared source-image references remain retained by the image.
\note This changes the image seen by all existing references to it.
\code{.js}
// image is an existing image; saved is a MemBlock from an image snapshot.
const reader = new pdg.Deserializer();
reader.setDataPtr(saved);
image.deserialize(reader);
\endcode
\sa Image::serialize(), Serializer::setResourceMode()
*/

/** \fn number Image::getMyClassTag()
\brief Return the native serialization class identifier for images.
\return The image class tag, shared by Image and ImageStrip.
*/
